// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Lieutenant_Harriman 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Lieutenant Harriman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P884274498" "Lieutenant Harriman"
// ProfessionString :
"P4164052128" "Sky Raider Squad Leader"
// DescriptionString :
"P4144389133" "Lieutenant Harriman's place in the Sky Raider hierarchy has been shaky at best. When Colonel Duray was captured after the assault of Skyway City, the Sky Raiders were left without a leader and with no clear guidelines for succession. Captain Castillo managed to rally the majority of the Raiders to his command, bolstered by his prior repute and his insistence that he was in command only 'until the Colonel returns.' Lieutenant Harriman, being Castillo's right hand man, was instantly lifted to a place in the Raiders' pecking order that far exceeded his actual rank. He intends to prove that he is capable and qualified for this new level of command, for the sake of his men and his peers - but most of all, for the sake of his captain."
// LocationString :
"P2093761884" "Nerva Archipelago"
// InteractionRequiresText :
"P3021462245" "<color orange>In order to play Lieutenant Harriman's storyarc, you must be either a Villain or Rogue, and will need to have purchased the second episode of the second signature story arc, <i>Pandora's Box</i>, or be a VIP subscriber."
// TaskForceInvite :
"P1785175189" "<color orange>Lieutenant Harriman snaps out an angry salute at you before speaking.</color><br><br>{HeroName}. My captain has informed me that you have purchased our services for the time being, and I've been ordered to work with you on tracking down the artifact called Pandora's Box.<br><br><color orange>Harriman spits on the ground.</color><br><br>Frankly, I think it's a load of crap, but when the captain says 'Jump-bots,' I say 'how many?' So I guess despite the fact that you assaulted my squad and stole our flagship, I have to play nice with you.<br><br>Problem is, I wouldn't know the first thing about ancient artifacts or any of that magical mystical mumbo-jumbo. I specialize in more modern hardware, understand? Still, I think I might have a lead."
// PlayerLevelTooLow :
"P564090246" "I can't believe this. Are you playing some kinda game here? I got taken down by some Rogue Isles goon that isn't even level 35? This has got to be some kind of joke, right?"
// PlayerLevelTooHigh :
// NeedLargeTeam :
// NeedTeamLeader :
"P544670376" "Look, pal, I'm not usually one for protocol, but I don't take messages from errand {Hero.gender=male boys|girls}. When your commander is ready to talk, I'll be here."
// NeedTeamOnMap :
"P333936829" "What is this, amateur hour? Where's your squad? Do you Rogue Isles types get anything done with this level of discipline?"
// BadTeamLevel :
"P970335761" "Whoa there, buddy. Your team's looking a little green, understand? I'll work with you, but I need the tools that don't break, and anyone under level 35 just isn't going to cut it."
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// TaskForceName :
// HelloString :
"P3063169384" "The sooner this assignment ends, the better."
// IDontKnowYouString :
// NoTasksRemainingString :
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
// FailsafeLevelString :
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


